SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00005322> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002202> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00005319>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00005326> (stomodeal invagination)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0089570") Annotation(rdf:type owl:Axiom) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00005326> "Infolding of the anteroventral embryo that arises during stage 10 (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). Its formation begins when cells surrounding the stomodeal anlage, which consists of a plate of tall cylindrical cells just prior to invagination, divide synchronously (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). The invaginated cells divide immediately afterwards, forming a monolayered epithelium (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It is initially oriented perpendicular to the horizontal plane, but progressively bends towards the ventral plane (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997). It grows caudally by cell divisions and incorporation of neighboring ectodermal cells (Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997).")
