# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047837> (embryonic/larval ensheathing glial cell)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0214261") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0229106") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0239943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0251788") Annotation(rdf:type owl:Axiom) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047837> "Ensheathing glial cell of the larva. There are approximately 112 of these cells in the third instar central nervous system (Pogodalla et al., 2021). Some of these cells are polyploid, but others can undergo cell division during the pupal stage to generate adult glia (Kato et al., 2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00047837> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705>)
