# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00049827> (larval gamma Kenyon cell)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0111409") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0218649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0255928") Annotation(rdf:type owl:Axiom) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00049827> "Gamma Kenyon cell of the larval (or late embryonic) mushroom body. It innervates both (vertical and medial) lobes (Lee et al., 1999; Kunz et al., 2012). It is the first type of Kenyon cell to be produced, and is born in the late embryo or early larva (Lee et al., 1999; Kunz et al., 2012). It is pruned back during early pupal stages to innervate only the gamma lobe of the adult mushroom body (Lee et al., 1999; Truman et al., 2023).")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00049827> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1373-1705>)
